# Environment for the SHARED MLMP instance — one container serving every
# visitor.
#
# THIS APP READS NOTHING FROM HERE. It is Caddy serving a directory of static
# files: a project overview, a trace player over committed fixtures, and a
# WebAssembly planner that runs entirely in the visitor's browser. There is no
# database, no account, no per-visitor state and no outbound call, which is why
# `mode: "shared"` is correct rather than merely cheap — the planning happens on
# the visitor's own CPU, not in this container.
#
# Copy this file to mlmp.shared.env on the VPS anyway. The broker starts the app
# without it (it logs `no env file at …` and carries on), but
# `gateway/deploy.sh` reports MISSING for every manifest service that has no env
# file, and a permanent MISSING is noise that hides a real one.
#
#   cp mlmp.shared.env.example mlmp.shared.env
#   chown root:1000 mlmp.shared.env && chmod 640 mlmp.shared.env
#
# No GATEWAY_SECRET: that exists so an app can tell the broker's identity
# headers from a client's. This app serves the same bytes to everyone and reads
# no header, so a secret here would be a value with nothing to protect.

TZ=UTC
